@doc smysl/0.1 {
  id: v/f7
  intent: merged-review
  lang: en
  granularity: { profile: default }
  roots: [f/verdict]
}

@evidence e/queue-depth { status: measured, source: { kind: metric, ref: "broker.queue_depth{topic=orders}", captured: 2026-07-18 } }
~ Queue depth on the orders topic rose from 40 to 12 000 over six minutes.

Sampled every fifteen seconds from the broker's own exporter, across all three
partitions, with the rise beginning four minutes after the consumer group was
restarted and continuing until the group was scaled out again.

@evidence e/consumer-lag { status: measured, source: { kind: metric, ref: "consumer.lag{group=orders-v2}", captured: 2026-07-18 } }
~ Consumer lag tracked queue depth exactly over the same window.

Measured per partition; all three moved together, which rules out a single
slow partition as the cause.

@claim c/consumers-undersized { status: derived, grounds: [e/queue-depth, e/consumer-lag] }
~ The consumer group could not keep up with the offered rate.

Lag that tracks depth rather than lagging behind it is the signature of a group
that is saturated rather than stalled, and the group had been sized for the
pre-migration rate that the orders topic no longer runs at.

@claim c/restart-was-trigger { status: inferred, grounds: [e/queue-depth] }
~ The restart began the backlog rather than causing the shortfall.

@evidence e/cpu-headroom { status: measured, source: { kind: metric, ref: "consumer.cpu{group=orders-v2}", captured: 2026-07-18 } }
~ Consumer CPU sat at 94 per cent throughout.

@claim c/not-io-bound { status: derived, grounds: [e/cpu-headroom] }
~ The bottleneck is processing, not downstream I/O.

CPU saturated while downstream call latency stayed flat, so the queue is not
waiting on anything outside the consumer.

@hypothesis h/broker-fault { status: speculative }
~ A broker-side fault could produce the same depth curve.

@claim c/brokers-healthy { status: derived, grounds: [e/cpu-headroom] }
~ Broker health metrics were unremarkable for the whole window.

@finding f/verdict { status: inferred, grounds: [c/consumers-undersized, c/not-io-bound] }
~ The orders consumer group is undersized for its current offered rate.

@rel c/brokers-healthy --rebuts--> h/broker-fault { weight: 0.7 }
@rel c/restart-was-trigger --causes--> c/consumers-undersized
@rel e/consumer-lag --backs--> c/consumers-undersized
